================================================================================
ENGAWA — ENhanced Galactic Atmospheres With Arepo
Public data release
================================================================================

A suite of cosmological zoom-in simulations that resolves the circumgalactic
medium (CGM) of four Milky Way-like galaxies down to 200 pc, using fixed-volume
mesh refinement in Arepo together with the IllustrisTNG feedback model. The
refinement caps the physical size of gas cells throughout the CGM rather than
tracking mass, holding 200 pc resolution from the disk out to 100 kpc. Stellar
ionizing radiation is added in post-processing with the COLT radiative-transfer
code.

  Website   https://www.scottlucchini.com/engawa/
            (overview, galaxy and resolution tables, figures, access guide)

  Paper     Lucchini, Abramson, Hummels, Conroy, Hernquist & Smith (2026),
            submitted to ApJ.  arXiv:2603.05584

  Contact   Scott Lucchini <scott.lucchini@cfa.harvard.edu>


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE GALAXIES  (z = 0 properties)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Dir     Origin           M*          M200         R200     Finest run
                           (1e10 Msun) (1e12 Msun)  (kpc)
  ------  ---------------  ----------  -----------  -------  ----------
  Au6     Auriga halo 6           4.8         1.04      214     200 pc
  Au8     Auriga halo 8           3.0         1.08      216     500 pc
  TNGA    TNG50 subhalo           5.2         1.02      212     200 pc
          (537941)
  TNGB    TNG50 subhalo           9.2         1.39      236     500 pc
          (519311)

Auriga masses are from Grand et al. (2017); TNG values are from the public halo
catalog. The galaxies themselves are consistent between resolution levels —
stellar masses agree to within 4% at z = 0.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESOLUTION LEVELS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Run       Refinement        V_target (kpc^3)   Spatial resolution
  --------  ----------------  ----------------   ------------------
  Default   Mass-based only   —                  TNG50-1 fiducial
  1kpc      + fixed volume    1.0                1 kpc
  500pc     + fixed volume    0.125              500 pc
  200pc     + fixed volume    0.015              200 pc  (Au6, TNGA only)

The target volume is applied inside a comoving radius R_ri = 100 ckpc and tapers
to the default scheme by R_ro = 200 ckpc; inside 0.15 R200 the disk/ISM stays at
the fiducial TNG50-1 resolution. Refinement is switched on at z = 0.3 and run for
3.4 Gyr to z = 0.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DIRECTORY LAYOUT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note that Au6 nests each run under its own output/, while the other three fold
the run into the directory name.

  /
  |-- Au6/
  |   |-- Default/output/
  |   |   |-- allclouds/               cloud catalog (Au6 only)
  |   |   |-- colt/                    COLT outputs, colt_NNN.hdf5
  |   |   |-- fof_subhalo_tab_NNN.hdf5 Subfind catalog (Default runs only)
  |   |   |-- fof_tab_NNN.hdf5         FOF catalog
  |   |   |-- snap_NNN.hdf5            snapshot
  |   |   `-- cpu.txt, energy.txt, ... Arepo run logs
  |   |-- 1kpc/output/
  |   |-- 500pc/output/                (also has output_rerun/)
  |   `-- 200pc/output/
  |-- Au8/
  |   |-- output_default/
  |   |-- output_1kpc/
  |   `-- output_500pc/
  |-- TNGA/
  |   |-- output_default/
  |   |-- output_1kpc/
  |   |-- output_500pc/
  |   `-- output/                      (the 200 pc run)
  `-- TNGB/
      |-- output_default/
      |-- output_1kpc/
      `-- output_500pc/

Every run directory follows the same pattern as the expanded one above. In the
Default runs each snapshot and catalog is a single file; in the refined runs they
are split across 64 files, held in snapdir_NNN/ and groups_NNN/ directories
instead. Subfind catalogs are present for the Default runs. Au6's COLT files are
split by escape fraction (e.g. colt_139_25fesc.hdf5).


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SNAPSHOT NUMBERING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All Default runs contain 140 snapshots following output_list_default.txt (every
50 Myr at late times). The 1 kpc and 200 pc runs use the same spacing and run
from 069-139. The 500 pc runs add snapshots every 10 Myr and run from 069-422.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNITS AND FIELDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Snapshots and group catalogs follow the IllustrisTNG conventions — the same
field names, unit system (comoving, h-scaled code units), and header layout. See
the TNG data specification for the full description:

  https://www.tng-project.org/data/docs/specifications/


